{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515197-tales-from-the-crypt-as-inspiration","id":1515197,"title":"Tales from the Crypt as Inspiration.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-15T18:51:39-07:00","id":1515197,"title":"Tales from the Crypt as Inspiration.","content":"When we first got V:tM, <i>Tales from the Crypt</i> was on, every Saturday-night, at 11:00, we watched it every weekend when we would RPG. I didn't draw inspiration because, I was new to the game and I wasn't running. But now, I just realized that I should have (well, drawn more). I just thought of every interaction with mortals the vampire-players have, mostly extended, where the mortals always try to murder the vampires. Not because they are vampires, but because they mortals want to rob them, use them or take their wealth. <br /> <br /> As anyone used media was inspiration for a vampire-game and how'd it go?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T21:28:04-07:00","id":1515202,"title":"","content":"Are not <b>They Came From Beyond the Grave</b> the natural RPG for <b>Tales of the Crypt </b>emulation? If I remember correctly, <b>Tales</b> did not have any major vampire elements. ( Well, they can be one or two episodes based on vampirism in original series? )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T00:40:31-07:00","id":1515216,"title":"","content":"The theme music is playing in my head like crazy now. <br /> <br /> <br /> Running along the lines of WoD's parodies of real world companies, I feel like the WoD would have had some kind of Tales from the Crypt show but the host would've been a Samedi or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T02:02:39-07:00","id":1515220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As anyone used media was inspiration for a vampire-game and how'd it go? </div> </div> </div>Assuming this means any media, not <i>Tales from the Crypt</i> specifically (I'm afraid I've never seen it) one of the first things that pops into my head when thinking of VtM inspiration, for some reason, is <i>Blackadder*.</i> (It's not the <i>exact </i>tone, but it's along those lines. Copious amounts of sarcasm; &quot;cunning plans&quot;; narcissism; your boss is a member of the corrupt elite making your life a pain (or your father/sire is); you feel like you're surrounded by idiots; <i>&quot;Do you have someone special in your life?&quot;-&quot;Well, yes, as a matter of fact, I do.&quot;-&quot;Who?&quot;-&quot;Me.&quot;-&quot;No, I mean someone you love, cherish and want to keep safe from all the horror and the hurt.&quot;-&quot;...Still me.&quot;</i>; and in the tune of the ending of Blackadder Goes Fourth, you are very, <i>very</i> expendable.)<br /> <br /> Then sprinkle in some GTA, VtM:B, whatever horror films my family was watching in my periphery last night that I absorbed my osmosis, and other stuff I can't specifically think of right now, or don't want to mention because it's a vampire shoujo manga intrinsically tied to my cringey mid-teens.<br /> Our games are 75% irreverent black comedy messes; with at least one sudden yet inevitable sharp 180\u00b0 turn into tragedy and horror somewhere down the line.<br /> <br /> * And I may or may not have planned a game that involves one of the unfortunate pcs getting saddled with the role of Scourge/executioner and their social life taking a hit from it (and of course the Prince uncovers new information about some plot or other that's important to them, which means that somebody the new Scourge<i> just executed</i> is vital to the Prince's plans and she won't be happy.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T09:04:20-07:00","id":1515255,"title":"","content":"We have used Mick Farren horror novels as a source of inspiration for some of our older games along with the Family Dracul series of novels that served as a prequal to Bram Stoker's Count Dracula and it worked great in explaining how coteries could work and how easy it is break the masquerade with even simple mistakes and it helped fleshed out our characters desires.<br /> <br /> Now a days it has expanded to other genres such as Brad Thor spy novels for the sense of desperation in a world where everyone has a phone or computer on there person and hunters could use that tech to great effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T17:18:33-07:00","id":1515317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515197-tales-from-the-crypt-as-inspiration?p=1515202#post1515202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are not <b>They Came From Beyond the Grave</b> the natural RPG for <b>Tales of the Crypt </b>emulation? If I remember correctly, <b>Tales</b> did not have any major vampire elements. ( Well, they can be one or two episodes based on vampirism in original series? )</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no doubt that it is and that it's excellent, but, since I learned V:tM and <i>Tales from the Crypt</i> at the same time, the ST-system in thoroughly in my mind. We did have <i>Cyberpunk's Night Edge</i>, at that time too, but nah. <br /> <br /> I'm just thinkin' that every long-term interaction with a mortal-NPC, they try and kill the PCs for money, power, or lust etc. For instance, I saw Treat William's role in a TftC, episode (directed by Tom Hanks), in which his character befriended, married and killed old-women (for their money), but, they came back to life (which, they didn't explain just how, but hinted on the con-mans ability of true-love).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T17:30:44-07:00","id":1515318,"title":"","content":"Big fan of the show. I remember watching Kids in the Hall then followed by Tales from the Crypt on HBO. Now I must rewatch it.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T00:28:03-07:00","id":1515332,"title":"","content":"I did not seen many episodes of Tales from the Crypt on HBO, but I did see a lot of episodes of Tales from the Darkside and its follow up series Monsters in syndication.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mioevxb2CfA\" data-code=\"Mioevxb2CfA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Mioevxb2CfA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I've always had a lot of love of the old anthology series ever since I saw the Twilight Zone episodes.<br /> <br /> In terms of inspiration, I don't think there was anything directly taken, but I think I absorbed a lot of atmosphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T10:15:47-07:00","id":1515397,"title":"","content":"Tales Of The Darkside I completely forgot about that series when I was a kid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T02:55:29-07:00","id":1515638,"title":"","content":"<i>Friday the 13th: The Series</i> was always an influence, both in the ubiquitous presence of creepy old antique stores in my WoD, and a lot of cursed objects that tended to have dark histories and would come back to bite their users.<br /> <br /> Also, a lot of the scripts for those anthology shows (The Twilight Zone, Outer Limits, Tales from the Darkside, Night Gallery, Ray Bradbury Theater, etc.) were adapted from existing short stories, some as far back as the Victorian period. Trying to find them and read them (in the pre internet era) led to me becoming a voracious reader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 06-20-2023, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T06:16:02-07:00","id":1515651,"title":"","content":"<i>Tales from the Crypt</i>\u200b, no<br /> But lately shamelessly ripped of the SCP Foundation<br /> (like SCP-610: The Flesh that Hates and the Sarkicism/Sarkite cults as a Tzimsice/Vicissitude infestation or SCP-035: Possessive Mask as a Harbringer of Skulls/Wraith Artefact and SCP-001: The Scarlet King as the one of the manace the Baali worship and tries to drag in to our word)<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}